WEBVTT

00:08:28.921 --> 00:08:31.090
At which point Kyle,
the manager of the shop,

00:08:31.131 --> 00:08:32.967
stepped in, he’s such a sweetheart.

00:08:32.967 --> 00:08:35.511
He said, “I think you’re probably right.

00:08:35.553 --> 00:08:36.887
Let me ask you a question.

00:08:37.304 --> 00:08:40.015
Do you only get a chirp
coming from that rear brake

00:08:40.057 --> 00:08:41.684
when you're pulling hard uphill?"

00:08:41.725 --> 00:08:43.394
I said, "Yes, exactly."

00:08:43.435 --> 00:08:45.771
He said, "Yeah, that's frame fatigue."

00:08:46.397 --> 00:08:50.442
I wanted to fall at the feet
of Kyle and call him blessed.

00:08:50.484 --> 00:08:51.652
(Laughter)

00:08:51.694 --> 00:08:54.947
Someone was taking me seriously.

00:08:54.947 --> 00:08:56.991
This happens all the time now.

00:08:56.991 --> 00:08:59.827
I have to go three
or four rounds with someone

00:08:59.868 --> 00:09:01.787
before I get a direct answer.